      "content": "so when you say \"choosing to stop,\" you mean like... a final choice? because i feel like if he just keeps living and suffering, it's just a loop of endless pain. a character who actually finds peace by making a definitive choice to end it... wouldn't that be more profound? like, instead of just fading away, he's actually taking control of his own ending? i just feel like that's the only way the story reaches a real, honest conclusion.",
